# --- Godot 4 ---
godot/.godot/
godot/export_presets.cfg
*.translation

# --- Node (engine-server) ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Runtime encounter save -- regenerated by seedState()/saveState() on first run;
# not something to track in git any more than the 2D app's own browser-side
# encounter autosave is. *.json.bak is saveState()'s own last-known-good backup
# copy (added alongside its atomic-write fix) -- a gap in this entry originally:
# `*.json` doesn't match a `.bak`-suffixed filename, so the backup showed up as
# a real untracked file the first time saveState() actually wrote one.
engine-server/state/*.json
engine-server/state/*.json.bak
!engine-server/state/.gitkeep

# Adventure map import (ROADMAP.md, 2026-09-19) -- a DM's own real map images
# (rasterized adventure-module pages, etc.), placed here by hand per
# MapImagePath.gd's own convention. Same "runtime/DM-provided data, not source"
# reasoning as encounter.json above, plus real licensing stakes this time (see
# CAMPAIGN_MAP_IMPORT_REPORT.md's Licensing section) -- never commit these.
engine-server/state/maps/*
!engine-server/state/maps/.gitkeep

# Phase 7: runtime request/response files this server and dm-bridge/watch.js write at
# play time (combat narration) -- generated locally, never meant to be committed. Same
# entry, same reasoning, as Campaign-OS's own .gitignore for its identical dm-bridge/
# folder -- these accidentally got committed once already (a live test session's real
# request/response) before this entry existed; that commit was reverted.
dm-bridge/*.json

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Creatures/ raw pack dumps + flattened copies ---
# Two different reasons live in this one ignored tree now, not just one:
# - The Quaternius packs (hero-pack/, monster-pack/, animation-library/'s
#   Universal Animation Library folders) are QAL v1.0 licensed
#   (https://quaternius.com/license.html) -- free to USE here, but section
#   3(a) prohibits redistributing the raw asset files themselves, so they
#   stay local-only rather than risk that via a git clone.
# - The KayKit packs living inside those SAME folders (hero-pack/
#   KayKit_Adventurers_*, monster-pack/KayKit_Skeletons_*, animation-library/
#   KayKit_Character_Animations_*) are genuinely CC0 -- no license reason to
#   exclude them at all. They're swept up by this same blanket ignore purely
#   for convenience (they share a parent folder with QAL content) and repo
#   hygiene (each raw download bundles FBX/OBJ/glTF variants of everything at
#   once) -- not because they need to be. Un-ignore/flatten specific KayKit
#   files the same way creatures/hero and creatures/monster already do for
#   Quaternius once a real model is actually wired up.
# Kenney's dungeon-kit is separate and NOT covered by any of this -- it's CC0
# and committed directly (see godot/assets/README.md).
godot/assets/Creatures/
godot/assets/creatures/

# --- Unused format variants from the Kenney dungeon-kit download ---
# CC0 like the rest of that pack (no license reason to exclude these) -- only
# ignored as plain repo hygiene, since this project only ever loads the GLB
# format (see GridManager.gd) and the FBX/OBJ copies + preview images are dead
# weight nobody will load. Remove this entry if you'd rather just keep everything.
godot/assets/Environment/dungeon-kit/Models/FBX format/
godot/assets/Environment/dungeon-kit/Models/OBJ format/
godot/assets/Environment/dungeon-kit/Previews/

# --- Exact duplicate of dungeon-kit above (same "Mini Dungeon (2.0)" pack,
# re-downloaded under a different folder name by mistake) -- zero new content,
# not worth tracking at all. Safe to delete this folder from disk entirely
# whenever convenient; kept out of git in the meantime.
godot/assets/Environment/kenney-dungeon/

# --- Quaternius environment MegaKits (Fantasy Props, Medieval Village,
# Stylized Nature) -- Phase 4 map-building material. Unlike the Creatures/
# packs above, these are genuinely CC0 (confirmed by reading each pack's own
# License_Standard.txt directly -- not every Quaternius pack uses the same
# license, so don't assume from the Creatures/ precedent above). Ignored here
# purely as repo hygiene, same reasoning as the Kenney FBX/OBJ entries: each
# raw download ships the same ~100-170 models in FBX/OBJ/glTF/Textures all at
# once, most of which won't end up used in any given hand-built map. Once a
# specific piece is actually used, flatten just that file into a clean path
# under godot/assets/environment/ (lowercase, mirroring creatures/hero and
# creatures/monster's own pattern) and commit that -- these three folders can
# be un-ignored instead if you'd rather just keep everything.
godot/assets/Environment/quaternius-buildings/
godot/assets/Environment/quaternius-nature/
godot/assets/Environment/quaternius-props/

# --- KayKit Dungeon Remastered -- genuinely CC0 (confirmed directly), same
# repo-hygiene-only ignore reasoning as the Quaternius MegaKits above (a raw
# download bundling gltf/obj/texture variants of ~200 pieces at once).
godot/assets/Environment/kaykit-dundeons/

# --- Higgsfield "3D Jutsu" catalog imports (Phase 8) -- unlike Kenney/
# Quaternius/KayKit above, Higgsfield's own Terms of Use has no section
# covering the pre-made catalog specifically (checked directly, not assumed).
# Fine for this project's own private, non-commercial use (see ROADMAP.md's
# Phase 8 entry for the actual reasoning), but not something to distribute
# via a git clone without a clearer answer from Higgsfield first -- same
# "convenience AND caution" sweep-up as the Meshy-generated Orc content.
godot/assets/Environment/higgsfield-test/
